.TH std::copyable 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::copyable \- std::copyable

.SH Synopsis
Defined in header <concepts>
template< class T >

concept copyable =
std::copy_constructible<T> &&
std::movable<T> &&                     \fI(since C++20)\fP
std::assignable_from<T&, T&> &&
std::assignable_from<T&, const T&> &&

std::assignable_from<T&, const T>;

The concept copyable<T> specifies that T is a movable object type that can also be copied
(that is, it supports copy construction and copy assignment).

.SH References

  * C++23 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2024):

           * 18.6 Object concepts [concepts.object]

  * C++20 standard (ISO/IEC 14882:2020):

           * 18.6 Object concepts [concepts.object]

.SH See also

movable specifies that an object of a type can be moved and swapped
(C++20) (concept)
